=== Part 1: >=3 defects => M >= 2/25  (the pinned crux, a LOWER bound) ===
  7785 families with >=3 defects; landed in gap (1/13,2/25): 0
  => lower bound holds in sample: >=3 defects => M >= 2/25.

=== Part 2: mod-25 covering reduction ===
  >=3-defect families: 7792; mod-25 clearable (=> M>=2/25 at t=c/25): 6001 (77%)
  non-mod-25 examples (clear elsewhere, M>>2/25; note 'has mult of 25'):
    [3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 17, 30, 35, 44, 50]: M=12/53 (denom 53), contains multiple of 25: True
    [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 20, 25, 30, 50]: M=2/11 (denom 11), contains multiple of 25: True
    [3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 11, 12, 34, 43, 50]: M=9/46 (denom 46), contains multiple of 25: True
    [1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 11, 12, 25, 30, 47]: M=2/17 (denom 17), contains multiple of 25: True
    [4, 8, 9, 10, 14, 19, 21, 24, 25, 29, 33, 37]: M=9/62 (denom 62), contains multiple of 25: True
    [3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 11, 13, 16, 22, 30, 50]: M=3/19 (denom 19), contains multiple of 25: True

  READING: the SHARP core of the crux = 'near-tight >=3-defect families are mod-25-clearable'
  (a FINITE covering-system statement, klein's leg). Non-clearable ones contain a multiple of
  25 (sits at residue 0 for every c) and clear at small denominators with M far above 2/25.
  => the Freiman residual is a mod-25 covering fact + an easy far-from-tight case.
